    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "So start simple. What is it, really?",
      "chapter": "The next-word machine"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "It's a large language model, or L L M. At its heart, it's a machine that guesses the next word.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "brain",
        "text": "LLM = large language model",
        "cue": "language",
        "sub": "a next-word guesser",
        "sub_cue": "guesses"
      },
      "punch": "guesses"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Guesses? Like when my phone suggests the next word in a text?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Same idea, but much bigger. Try it. If I say, peanut butter and, what comes next?",
      "board": {
        "type": "chat",
        "title": "FINISH IT",
        "color": "#0A84FF",
        "items": [
          {
            "who": "user",
            "text": "Peanut butter and…",
            "cue": "peanut"
          },
          {
            "who": "bot",
            "text": "jelly? jam?",
            "cue": "next"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Jelly! Or jam."
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "See? You didn't look it up. You've seen that pattern many times. The model learned patterns like that from a huge amount of text.",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "HOW YOU GUESSED",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": "Seen it many times",
            "icon": "eye",
            "cue": "seen"
          },
          {
            "label": "Spot the pattern",
            "icon": "target",
            "cue": "pattern"
          },
          {
            "label": "AI: huge amounts of text",
            "icon": "book",
            "cue": "huge"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "But it writes whole essays, not one word."
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Right, it just repeats the guess. Pick one word, add it, then guess again, and again, until the answer is done.",
      "board": {
        "type": "cycle",
        "title": "ONE WORD AT A TIME",
        "center": "✍️",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🔮",
            "label": "Guess",
            "cue": "guess"
          },
          {
            "icon": "👆",
            "label": "Pick one",
            "cue": "pick"
          },
          {
            "icon": "➕",
            "label": "Add it",
            "cue": "add"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🔁",
            "label": "Repeat",
            "cue": "again"
          }
        ],
        "color": "#0A84FF"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Wait, does it really read words like we do?",
      "chapter": "Tokens"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Not quite. It splits your text into small pieces called tokens. A token can be a whole word, part of a word, or even a comma.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🧩",
        "text": "Tokens = small pieces of text",
        "cue": "tokens"
      },
      "punch": "tokens"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Part of a word? Show me."
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "A long word such as unbelievable might be split into pieces, like un, believ, and able. The exact split depends on the tool.",
      "board": {
        "type": "gallery",
        "title": "UNBELIEVABLE →",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🧩",
            "label": "un",
            "cue": "like"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🧩",
            "label": "believ",
            "cue": "believ"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🧩",
            "label": "able",
            "cue": "able"
          }
        ],
        "color": "#8E44AD"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "And then it reads the pieces?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Each token is turned into numbers. Computers are great with numbers, so the model does math on them to find patterns between the tokens.",
      "board": {
        "type": "journey",
        "title": "TEXT TO NUMBERS",
        "traveler": "🧩",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🔤",
            "label": "Tokens",
            "cue": "token"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🔢",
            "label": "Numbers",
            "cue": "numbers"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🧮",
            "label": "Math",
            "cue": "math"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🔗",
            "label": "Patterns",
            "cue": "patterns"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "So where did it learn all these patterns?",
      "chapter": "How it learned"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "First comes training. It practiced on a huge amount of text, like books and websites, guessing hidden next words over and over.",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "STEP 1: TRAINING",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": "Huge amount of text",
            "icon": "book",
            "cue": "huge"
          },
          {
            "label": "Guess the hidden word",
            "icon": "🙈",
            "cue": "guessing"
          },
          {
            "label": "Over and over",
            "icon": "🔁",
            "cue": "over"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "How does it know if a guess was right?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "The real next word is in the text, so it can check! When it guesses wrong, its settings get adjusted a tiny bit. Repeat that a huge number of times.",
      "board": {
        "type": "cycle",
        "title": "LEARNING LOOP",
        "center": "🧠",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🔍",
            "label": "Check",
            "cue": "check"
          },
          {
            "icon": "❌",
            "label": "Wrong?",
            "cue": "wrong"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🔧",
            "label": "Adjust a bit",
            "cue": "adjusted"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🔁",
            "label": "Repeat",
            "cue": "repeat"
          }
        ],
        "color": "#2ECC71"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "And then it's ready to chat?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Not yet. Next, people give it example conversations and rate its answers, so it learns to be more helpful and safer.",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "STEP 2: TUNING",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": "Example chats",
            "icon": "chat",
            "cue": "example"
          },
          {
            "label": "People rate answers",
            "icon": "👍",
            "cue": "rate"
          },
          {
            "label": "More helpful & safer",
            "icon": "shield",
            "cue": "helpful"
          }
        ],
        "color": "#E91E63"
      },
      "punch": "rate"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "So it's basically read a library and had a coach."
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Ha, nice way to put it! A library for language patterns, and a coach for manners.",
      "board": {
        "type": "compare",
        "left": {
          "label": "LIBRARY",
          "color": "#0A84FF",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Language patterns",
