    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Okay, so what happens when I actually type a question?",
      "chapter": "From question to answer"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Let's follow it. Your question becomes tokens. The model looks at the whole chat, guesses the next token, and repeats until the answer is done.",
      "board": {
        "type": "journey",
        "title": "YOUR QUESTION'S TRIP",
        "traveler": "💬",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "❓",
            "label": "Question",
            "cue": "question"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🧩",
            "label": "Tokens",
            "cue": "tokens"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🔮",
            "label": "Next-word guesses",
            "cue": "guesses"
          },
          {
            "icon": "✅",
            "label": "Answer",
            "cue": "answer"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Does it always pick the most likely word?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Not always. There's a little randomness, so it can pick a likely word that isn't the top one. That's why the same question can get different answers.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🎲",
        "text": "A bit of randomness",
        "cue": "randomness",
        "sub": "same question, different answers",
        "sub_cue": "different"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Huh. So asking twice could give me two versions."
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Yep! It also reads the whole chat so far. So if you mention your dog early on, it can use that later in the same chat.",
      "board": {
        "type": "chat",
        "title": "IT READS THE CHAT",
        "color": "#2ECC71",
        "items": [
          {
            "who": "user",
            "text": "My dog loves long walks.",
            "cue": "dog"
          },
          {
            "who": "bot",
            "text": "Try a park trail with your dog!",
            "cue": "later"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "So it remembers everything about me forever?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Not by default. A new chat usually starts fresh, unless the tool has a memory feature. And very long chats can lose track of early details.",
      "board": {
        "type": "checklist",
        "title": "MEMORY",
        "icon": "brain",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "New chat starts fresh",
            "cue": "new",
            "ok": true
          },
          {
            "text": "Some tools have memory",
            "cue": "memory",
            "ok": true
          },
          {
            "text": "Long chats lose track",
            "cue": "long",
            "ok": false
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "So does it understand me like a person does?",
      "chapter": "What it can't do"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Not like a person. It's amazing with language, but it has no feelings or life experience. Scientists still debate what it really understands.",
      "board": {
        "type": "compare",
        "left": {
          "label": "GREAT AT",
          "color": "#0A84FF",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Language",
              "icon": "chat",
              "cue": "language",
              "tick": true
            }
          ]
        },
        "right": {
          "label": "DOESN'T HAVE",
          "color": "#FF4D6D",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Feelings",
              "icon": "❤️",
              "cue": "feelings",
              "tick": false
            },
            {
              "text": "Life experience",
              "icon": "🌍",
              "cue": "experience",
              "tick": false
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Can it be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Definitely. It's built to sound likely, not to check facts. So it can say something false in a very confident voice.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "warn",
        "text": "Sounds likely ≠ true",
        "cue": "likely"
      },
      "punch": "confident"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Does it know today's news?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Only what was in its training text, which stops at a certain date. Some tools can search the web, so check if yours does.",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "TODAY'S NEWS?",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": "Learned up to a date",
            "icon": "calendar",
            "cue": "training"
          },
          {
            "label": "Some tools search the web",
            "icon": "globe",
            "cue": "search"
          },
          {
            "label": "Check yours",
            "icon": "check",
            "cue": "check"
          }
        ],
        "color": "#FF8C42"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "So for anything important..."
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Use it as a smart helper, then double-check facts that matter, like health, money or school work.",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "USE IT WISELY",
